{
 "rule": "THE RULE (the rows no one has tuned). Sun height h(m) = emax * sin(pi * (m - 330) / 900) between sunrise 05:30 and sunset 20:30 (solar noon 13:00 falls\nout at m = 780), emax = the world's 13:00 elevation; s = h / emax (1 at noon, 0.588 at 17:30). v = (1 - s) / (1 - 0.588) is how far the sun is\nfrom its noon height towards its 17:30 height, the same before and after noon.\n  sun colour, ambient, wall, spec, fill, shift, al, fog: noon row -> 17:30 row by min(v, 1) (a morning mirrors its evening), except the ends:\n  06:30 and 19:30 take DAWN and SUNSET in the elf world (a low sun that is red on the open ground, a shade that keeps its colour, light enough to read); the hour between a\n  key and the mirrored colours (07:30 between DAWN and 08:30, 18:30 between 17:30 and SUNSET) is the straight mix of the two.\n  below the 17:30 height the sun colour and `al` fade to 0 with s / 0.588 and the ambient falls towards the night ambient by 1 - s / 0.588.\n  shadow lean sl = sl13 -/+ (sl17 - sl13) * v, length sq = sq13 + (sq17 - sq13) * v (lean negative before noon: the morning leans left).\n  elevation = h (at least 0.05); the light's direction L keeps its 13:00 / 17:30 heading, turned the same way, one turn per day.\n  night rows (sun down): sun a hundredth of the 17:30 sun, `al` 0 (no sun shadow, the cast table has no key there), ambient = the night ambient\n  = the 17:30 ambient x (0.30, 0.34, 0.52), in the elf world x (0.345, 0.39, 0.60) (tuned on the column: its wild night at 00:00 within 3 levels\n  of the classic valley's); sunset and sunrise rows have `al` 0 so a shadow fades out instead of vanishing.",
